      'In ADIF files with a damaged field (wrong length, unclosed descriptor, record without an end) only that field is lost, not the rest of the file; a second callsign in the same record no longer mixes with the fields of the first one, and the tail of a file with no record end no longer merges with the next file. JT65 safely refuses invalid erasures, and in Fox the special callsign CLEARALL! clears the scores.',
